## Repo layout (opinionated, monorepo)

```
hyperfocus-zone/
├─ .github/                     # CI workflows, issue/pr templates, actions
├─ infra/                       # infra-as-code (terraform / k8s / cloud)
├─ services/                    # deployable services / microservices
│  ├─ web-portal/               # Next.js / React site
│  ├─ api-gateway/              # API gateway / auth
│  ├─ agent-runner/             # orchestrates AI agents (Python)
│  ├─ bro-ski-bot/              # Discord bot (Node/Python)
│  └─ worker/                   # background jobs / schedulers
├─ libs/                        # shared libraries (JS, Python, Rust, etc.)
├─ tools/                       # developer tools and small CLIs
├─ packages/                    # optional: npm/pip packages for publishing
├─ experiments/                 # prototype & vibe-code quick builds
├─ docs/                        # docs, handbooks, onboarding, architecture
├─ assets/                      # logos, posters, video, stickers, fonts
├─ data/                        # small seed data / sample datasets
├─ backups/                     # encrypted snapshots (not in git; listed)
├─ .env.example
├─ docker-compose.yml
├─ Makefile
├─ README.md
└─ CODEOWNERS
```

### Per-service standard (use as a template)

```
services/<name>/
├─ src/
├─ tests/
├─ Dockerfile
├─ Makefile (or tasks)
├─ pyproject.toml / package.json
├─ .env.example
├─ README.md
└─ .github/ (optional: service-specific workflows)
```

Each service should expose a `/healthz` endpoint, structured logs, and Prometheus metrics when appropriate.

